<BaseLayout title="Our First Shared Budget Worksheet | DollarAngle" description="Free printable shared-budget worksheet for couples moving in together.">
<section class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:760px">
<div class="no-print"><p><a href="/articles/moving-in-together-money-rules">← Back to moving-in money guide</a></p><button type="button" onclick="window.print()">Print or save as PDF</button></div>
<article class="worksheet"><p class="brand">DOLLARANGLE • FREE WORKSHEET</p><h1>Our First Shared Budget</h1><p>A 30-minute money conversation before moving in together.</p>
<h2>1. Monthly take-home income</h2><p>Partner A: $____________________</p><p>Partner B: $____________________</p>
<h2>2. Shared monthly expenses</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Expense</th><th>Monthly amount</th></tr><tr><td>Rent</td><td>$____________</td></tr><tr><td>Utilities and internet</td><td>$____________</td></tr><tr><td>Groceries and supplies</td><td>$____________</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance, parking and transport</td><td>$____________</td></tr><tr><td>Other shared costs</td><td>$____________</td></tr><tr><th>Total</th><th>$____________</th></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>3. How we'll split costs</h2><p>☐ Equal (50/50)  ☐ Income-proportional  ☐ Another arrangement</p><p>Partner A contribution: $____________</p><p>Partner B contribution: $____________</p><h2>4. Before signing the lease</h2><p>☐ We agreed on payment dates and responsibility</p><p>☐ We discussed deposits, furniture and shared purchases</p><p>☐ We planned for income changes and emergencies</p><p>☐ We discussed what happens if someone moves out</p><p>☐ We chose a date to review this plan</p><p class="fine">General educational worksheet only. Legal obligations vary with lease terms and state law.</p>
</article></div></section>
